message: "If you reference this archive, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Self-Falsification as Method: A Cosmology Case Study"
abstract: >
  A serious-amateur exploration of Critical Null-Structured Cosmology
  (CNSC), a non-inflationary cosmological framework based on null
  hypersurface geometry, DBI-saturated kinetic action, and a 3D Ising-type
  phase transition.

  Conducted by an agricultural engineer as a personal theoretical-cosmology
  interest.  A systematic seven-weakness derivation program found that all
  of the framework's novel quantitative content is not mathematically
  derivable from the stated assumptions.  A successor framework
  ("framework v2", path-integral coherence VSL hypothesis) was outlined and
  tested by grid search; it was also found cosmologically unobservable at
  any parameter value.  Total: 8 negative outcomes, 0 surviving novel
  quantitative content.

  The most transferable artifact is the methodology M1-M8 codified in
  framework_v2/03_methodology.md, applicable to alternative-theory
  verification in any domain, including machine-learning model verification
  in the author's primary agricultural-engineering work.

  Not a peer-reviewed publication; an idea and methodology archive.
